{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul","id":968289,"title":"C20: Minor tweaks to a nostalgia product vs a more drastic overhaul?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-12T18:24:19-07:00","id":968289,"title":"C20: Minor tweaks to a nostalgia product vs a more drastic overhaul?","content":"In another thread a side conversation has developed about just how unworkable <i>Changeling: The Dreaming</i> was as a game and just how much of the 2nd Edition mechanics should be changed in the C20 edition. Now, I know the manuscript is either in editing or just completed editing, so there's no chance of this affecting C20 at all, which I'm fine with, but I was wondering what people thought generally about the nostalgia of simply giving <i>Changeling</i> the revised edition it never got plus a 20th anniversary update akin to the rest of the line vs actually overhauling the mechanics and making the game function better as a coherent whole.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think there's some charm to the almost schizophrenic / multiple personality / &quot;too many different directions&quot; nature of the rules. I'm hoping C20 is simply a smoothing of the edges and the bits of changes that should have appeared in the revised edition, plus the minor tweaks thanks to the 20th anniversary edition (in keeping with the other games and the minor tweaks they received when going from 2nd revised to 20th). But some disagree:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keichiokami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/964996-changelings-vs-the-rest-of-the-wod?p=968076#post968076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely disagree, I am looking forward to <i>Changeling</i> getting updated mechanics that reflect both the Revised edition it should have gotten, and an update using modern game design principles. All of indications and previews have pointed out that with C20, that will be the case.<br /> <br /> Nostalgia is awesome and all, but consider every CtD game I have played in both LARP and Tabletop has been *extensively* house ruled to be playable, I am sooooo ready for that not to be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, rather than continuing a thread derailment, let's have that conversation here.<br /> <br /> So, what do people think? Minor tweaks and updates, but mostly a nostalgia product that remains true to <i>Changeling</i> 2nd Edition, or a game that's more drastically updated and rules overhauled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11658,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","user":"Rabbit Pooka","date":". 09-12-2016, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T19:22:47-07:00","id":968312,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping for a balance of the 2. I want a game that feels like Changeling, even if the rules need to be changed somewhat to work better thematically.<br /> I do think a good portion of the rules need...something. Tweaking a lot of the time. Overhauling here and there. I'm really looking forward to the Arts/Realm mixtures since they are supposed to work better in C20 (have more actual viable combinations) than in CtD.<br /> <br /> I have faith in the people behind it and will await judgement until I see my book/pdf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T19:44:49-07:00","id":968321,"title":"","content":"Any attempt to smooth the edges for some people will be &quot;a drastic overhaul&quot;. We know for a fact before Changeling was cancelled it was going to get a drastic overhaul. Building in the book of Glamour into C20 is damned reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T20:17:47-07:00","id":968332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=968321#post968321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any attempt to smooth the edges for some people will be &amp;quot;a drastic overhaul&amp;quot;. We know for a fact before Changeling was cancelled it was going to get a drastic overhaul. Building in the book of Glamour into C20 is damned reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually what I was talking about in my original post. There was a lot of talk of overhauling the magic system in Book of Glamour shortly before the line was cancelled. I and the majority of the CtD fan community was genuinely excited for those upcoming changes.<br /> <br /> The idea of getting a solid update using Revised mechanics, the new overhauls to cantrips and glamour that were being planned, AND fresh new ideas to revitalize the game? Those ideas get me excited. From the various posts we have seen from the writers and developers that seems to be what C20 is going to be and I am so down.<br /> <br /> Do I want the game to be unrecognizeable? No of course not! It has a wonderful and rich setting, with awesome themes, that is why I feel in love with the game in the first place. But I am open to any and all mechanical updates they improve my enjoyment of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T01:30:19-07:00","id":968412,"title":"","content":"The setting changes appear to be minimal, from the excerpts we've seen. There are still the usual kiths, seemings, etc. The thallain seem to have expanded, but that's not a bad thing.<br /> <br /> From the excerpt we've seen, the magic system is much simpler (I didn't care for the example bunks given, but that was a matter of taste) and Unleashing is a huge boon. No more useless Arts. It also looks like some subsystems may have been codified as Arts (Invoking the Dragon's Ire, Contracts), which may or may not work, but seems a pretty reasonable idea.<br /> <br /> There's also a fifth way of gaining Glamour: Revelry, I think. This addresses the Glamour economy, although I wonder if Glamour will ever be as easy for changelings to regain as it is for Inanimae (the ability to meditate among the relevant element makes it easy to fudge the replenishing of Glamour).<br /> <br /> I do agree with others that it'll be good not to have to house rule everything. Glamour and magic were the big things to fix. The other Revised-era changes (bashing and lethal damage, new initiative and damage rules, tweaks to multiple actions, etc) were always easy enough to crib from other Revised books, so they're less valuable to the fixes to other systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 09-13-2016, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T09:23:55-07:00","id":968564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keichiokami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=968332#post968332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is actually what I was talking about in my original post. There was a lot of talk of overhauling the magic system in Book of Glamour shortly before the line was cancelled. I and the majority of the CtD fan community was genuinely excited for those upcoming changes.<br /> <br /> The idea of getting a solid update using Revised mechanics, the new overhauls to cantrips and glamour that were being planned, AND fresh new ideas to revitalize the game? Those ideas get me excited. From the various posts we have seen from the writers and developers that seems to be what C20 is going to be and I am so down.<br /> <br /> Do I want the game to be unrecognizeable? No of course not! It has a wonderful and rich setting, with awesome themes, that is why I feel in love with the game in the first place. But I am open to any and all mechanical updates they improve my enjoyment of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Lets look at infusion. Its an art that exists to paper over a hole in the system. Now lets say someone decided Infusion needed to go but replaced it with a full and readily available system for making chimera and treasures. Something anyone can do but Nockers are really good at. Some might say &quot;that's making the game unregognizeable!&quot; since they focused entirely on the idea of Nockers having a secret art that no one else could use.. yet some how everyone had Treasures.<br /> <br /> Let look at Title. This is something intrinsically upheld by the Dreaming in most books. Except in Kithbook Eshu where you can buy Title that white people can ignore but is totally cool In the Middle East/India/Africa. I find this a edge that needs to be cleaned up not other people would say &quot;that's unrecognizeable!&quot;<br /> <br /> We barely have any real cover outside North America, even going over the Kingdoms of Europe would be an almost unrecognizable difference even with the same players. <br /> <br /> Finally this is 20+ years later from the Resurgence, even assuming the metaplot its 17 years since the Second House coming, the Situation with teh Sidhe will have changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:33:39-07:00","id":968605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=968564#post968564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets look at infusion. Its an art that exists to paper over a hole in the system. Now lets say someone decided Infusion needed to go but replaced it with a full and readily available system for making chimera and treasures. Something anyone can do but Nockers are really good at. Some might say &quot;that's making the game unregognizeable!&quot; since they focused entirely on the idea of Nockers having a secret art that no one else could use.. yet some how everyone had Treasures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice example <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What about things that were totally ST discretion before, like Bedlam? Would it be better to keep it totally up to the ST or give rules so that players can see their characters becoming addicted to Glamour?<br /> <br /> What about something as fundamental as &quot;the present day?&quot; Would it be better assume the events in Denizens/War in Concordia/Book of Lost Houses are still the status quo or to assume it's now 2016 and stuff happened in the intervening years?<br /> <br /> C20 has an interesting tightrope to walk that V20, W20, and M20 didn't have to worry about \u2014 it's both an anniversary book and true new edition at the same time. Some things that stay the same might be leaving a broken mess to some folks. Some things that change might be making the game unrecognizable to others. Where that line is drawn will definitely vary from person to person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T12:46:08-07:00","id":968688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=968605#post968605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What about something as fundamental as &quot;the present day?&quot; Would it be better assume the events in Denizens/War in Concordia/Book of Lost Houses are still the status quo or to assume it's now 2016 and stuff happened in the intervening years?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alot of the intial setting of Changeling was defined by the Accordance war, but that was 27 years out and fading into the legends of Grumps.. now the Ressuregence and the Accordance war are well over 50 years ago, functionally its been two generations since then(changeling time can be wonky) the unique tying of Changeling to a real world time period forces somethings that other games don't have.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as I said earlier I'd love to see something more than &quot;Concordia&quot; yes the United states is the largest segment of the audience but at least cover something more..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 09-13-2016, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T14:30:25-07:00","id":968742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=968688#post968688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alot of the intial setting of Changeling was defined by the Accordance war, but that was 27 years out and fading into the legends of Grumps.. now the Ressuregence and the Accordance war are well over 50 years ago, functionally its been two generations since then(changeling time can be wonky) the unique tying of Changeling to a real world time period forces somethings that other games don't have.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as I said earlier I'd love to see something more than &amp;quot;Concordia&amp;quot; yes the United states is the largest segment of the audience but at least cover something more..</div> </div> </div> </div>God, yes! Britain, Ireland, France, Germany, Romania . . . There's so much faerie lore to be mined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:38:06-07:00","id":968899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=968742#post968742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> God, yes! Britain, Ireland, France, Germany, Romania . . . There's so much faerie lore to be mined.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well Britain and Ireland were theoretically covered.. I say in theory because Isle of the Mighty had as much in common with the Britain and the Rest fo the UK as Avalon from 7th Sea.<br /> <br /> Let me throw out there South America, it should have a similar history of imperalism, but we don't even know what the native Fae would even be called as a group.. maybe they did better intergrating? It would be a full on alien setting for Changeling as it was in 2e..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T00:00:17-07:00","id":969709,"title":"","content":"Sure, I'd love to see the setting expanded and updated, as I'm assuming it was for the other 20th lines. My concern was explicitly mechanical as Changeling was the youngest line with the most changes from 1st to 2nd, and the most that still needed work before being cancelled. But then I'm a firm believer that the mechanics matter and they invariably affect the way the game plays and the fiction created in play. I'm just concerned that there will be things missing (as hinted at by comments that some Arts just don't work like they used to), and that the need to nail down an exact system and mechanic for everything is a wonderfully Banal irony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T03:49:29-07:00","id":969801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=969709#post969709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, I'd love to see the setting expanded and updated, as I'm assuming it was for the other 20th lines. My concern was explicitly mechanical as Changeling was the youngest line with the most changes from 1st to 2nd, and the most that still needed work before being cancelled. But then I'm a firm believer that the mechanics matter and they invariably affect the way the game plays and the fiction created in play. I'm just concerned that there will be things missing (as hinted at by comments that some Arts just don't work like they used to), and that the need to nail down an exact system and mechanic for everything is a wonderfully Banal irony.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mechanics do matter. If Mechanics fail to support game concepts then thsoe mechanics are bad. There are alot of bad arts. Infusion, Talecraft, Onerimancy, Discord. Whoever made these arts didn't understand they weren't writing up Disciplines.<br /> <br /> <br /> And there's nothing more ironic than this :&quot; I'm a firm believer that the mechanics matter and they invariably affect the way the game plays and the fiction created in play.&quot; then complaining about the need to nail down an exact system for everything. Concepts in game without mechanical support twist the fiction either by nonexistence or are made up separately at the table and thus &quot;why am I paying for this&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:23:17-07:00","id":969850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=969709#post969709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as hinted at by comments that some Arts just don't work like they used to</div> </div> </div> </div>To set expectations \u2014 some Arts just don't work like they used to. These aren't the 2E core book Arts though. Chicanery, Legerdemain, Primal, Soothsay, Sovereign, and Wayfare are all there. Some of those have been smoothed out and had a level or two changed, but they're still basically the same Arts you knew before.<br /> <br /> It's the non-core book Arts that got reworked. Things like Skycraft are hopefully something players will actually want to take now. I love the new Arts. I think they serve certain character concepts that were always talked about in Changeling but never really given a solid way to be portrayed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":".  Clarity 09-15-2016, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T16:32:46-07:00","id":970303,"title":"","content":"There would've been a Treasure-Craft Art in the Book of Glamour, which was mentioned in a thread on Shadownessence. I hope we also get the Ravaging Art cut from Shadow Court and Pour L'Amour et Liberte.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:14:10-07:00","id":970470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=969801#post969801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanics do matter. If Mechanics fail to support game concepts then those mechanics are bad. There are a lot of bad arts. Infusion, Talecraft, Onerimancy, Discord. Whoever made these arts didn't understand they weren't writing up Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't argue with you there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And there's nothing more ironic than this :&quot; I'm a firm believer that the mechanics matter and they invariably affect the way the game plays and the fiction created in play.&quot; then complaining about the need to nail down an exact system for everything. Concepts in game without mechanical support twist the fiction either by nonexistence or are made up separately at the table and thus &quot;why am I paying for this&quot; </div> </div> </div>I think system does matter, but you don't need a system for everything. Especially things that either don't really matter, or that will easily lead to more focus on the mechanics themselves rather than the fiction being created at the table. For example, crafting chimera. It really doesn't need a full-blown system. From the fluff, any Changeling having a bad night can accidentally create a chimera. And artisans can intentionally craft their dreams into chimerical reality. What more do we need in terms of nailed down mechanics? Charts and tables, modifiers and ingredients? I don't think so.<br /> <br /> Take this as an example, a Nocker is tasked with making a chimerical sword for the duke. Okay. But the duke wants something special... say a sword crafted from the moonlight reflected off the fountain in Armstrong Park in New Orleans. But he's the Duke of New York. You can handle that as a quest to get the stuff and once that's successfully gathered up, you just craft the sword... or you can mechanize that and force a roll to actually make the thing. Which could fail. Is that the type of mundane banal reality that needs to be reflected in the mechanics? I don't think so.<br /> <br /> After a quest like that, crafting the sword should be a gimme. The fun and adventure and excitement of the quest itself is the exciting part...not in making a roll after all that, especially a roll that could be failed. This is a storytelling game. It's supposed to be about telling great stories at the table through play and later on about the play. The story you tell for years to come is about how you were chased out of Armstrong Park by a garou and had to use the pooka as bait to lure it away long enough to harvest the moonlight, not: &quot;Yep, rolled one success to craft the sword.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can hear people saying they're not mutually exclusive. I think they are, for the simple reason that having to make that roll after the quest undercuts the thing entirely. It focuses things in the wrong direction. It focuses play on the mechanics (whether you rolled well enough to craft the sword) instead of on the story about how you gathered up all the stuff on an epic road trip. It's the whiff factor, x100.<br /> <br /> The other drawback is munchkining the mechanics. Take crafting in most iterations of D&amp;D, you have charts and charts of weapons, crafting times, costs, etc. Most players and GMs think nothing of it till they get that one player to games the system. They spot that the cost of 100 arrows is about 100x the cost of crafting 100 arrows. So they start thinking of small businesses, franchise rights, and saving themselves a few coin on starting equipment. The Changeling version is skipping the Chimera background because the character's a Nocker and can just make their own. It doesn't sound like a big deal, but is that the kind of banal mundanity that should be reflected in the mechanics of C20? I don't think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:50:05-07:00","id":970480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=970470#post970470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't argue with you there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think system does matter, but you don't need a system for everything. Especially things that either don't really matter, or that will easily lead to more focus on the mechanics themselves rather than the fiction being created at the table. For example, crafting chimera. It really doesn't need a full-blown system. From the fluff, any Changeling having a bad night can accidentally create a chimera. And artisans can intentionally craft their dreams into chimerical reality. What more do we need in terms of nailed down mechanics? Charts and tables, modifiers and ingredients? I don't think so.<br /> <br /> Take this as an example, a Nocker is tasked with making a chimerical sword for the duke. Okay. But the duke wants something special... say a sword crafted from the moonlight reflected off the fountain in Armstrong Park in New Orleans. But he's the Duke of New York. You can handle that as a quest to get the stuff and once that's successfully gathered up, you just craft the sword... or you can mechanize that and force a roll to actually make the thing. Which could fail. Is that the type of mundane banal reality that needs to be reflected in the mechanics? I don't think so.<br /> <br /> After a quest like that, crafting the sword should be a gimme. The fun and adventure and excitement of the quest itself is the exciting part...not in making a roll after all that, especially a roll that could be failed. This is a storytelling game. It's supposed to be about telling great stories at the table through play and later on about the play. The story you tell for years to come is about how you were chased out of Armstrong Park by a garou and had to use the pooka as bait to lure it away long enough to harvest the moonlight, not: &quot;Yep, rolled one success to craft the sword.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can hear people saying they're not mutually exclusive. I think they are, for the simple reason that having to make that roll after the quest undercuts the thing entirely. It focuses things in the wrong direction. It focuses play on the mechanics (whether you rolled well enough to craft the sword) instead of on the story about how you gathered up all the stuff on an epic road trip. It's the whiff factor, x100.<br /> <br /> The other drawback is munchkining the mechanics. Take crafting in most iterations of D&amp;D, you have charts and charts of weapons, crafting times, costs, etc. Most players and GMs think nothing of it till they get that one player to games the system. They spot that the cost of 100 arrows is about 100x the cost of crafting 100 arrows. So they start thinking of small businesses, franchise rights, and saving themselves a few coin on starting equipment. The Changeling version is skipping the Chimera background because the character's a Nocker and can just make their own. It doesn't sound like a big deal, but is that the kind of banal mundanity that should be reflected in the mechanics of C20? I don't think so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You know what's banal? Another quest. I've quested in a thousand games. Gathering loot, gathering stupid little materials. Its boring. Its trite. You know who are true legends? Wayland Smith. Hatori Hanzo. Hephaestus. Emiya Shiro. The quest to become a legendary swordsmith is just as worthy of the Dreaming as the quest to forge a legendary sword, and to the Nocker player more so. To craft the stuff of Dreams, to craft the things of Legend these are his story and it is one worth say. You want to take his story and throw it to the hands of some murder hobo who can steal the right item.<br /> <br /> There's nothing more banal than spitting in the face of an entire Kith's Dream saying its &quot;Boring&quot; and pointless. Unless its Bogans cause their dream is &quot;barter Economy&quot;(J/k)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:19:42-07:00","id":970493,"title":"","content":"No crafting subsystem = genocide of a kith. Yeah, coz that's a reasonable conclusion to draw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:40:58-07:00","id":970506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=970493#post970493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No crafting subsystem = genocide of a kith. Yeah, coz that's a reasonable conclusion to draw.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No. I'm saying No crafting system spits in the face of the Kith's concept. Each and every issue you have with a Crafting system could be applied to any other system. &quot;We went of a quest and the nocker failed to smith our sword what bullshit&quot; is no different than &quot;We went on a quest and the Sluagh failed to sneak up on a dragon and we lost&quot; or &quot;We challenged the evil Duke.. and he beat us with swords what bullshit&quot;<br /> <br /> You think Crafting was the place for munchkining not.. COMBAT in D&amp;D? <br /> <br /> <br /> A system is only as boring as you make it. You say its dramatic to go in a quest. I say the drama is in the forge. To do the impossible by the skin of your teeth to become a person who can craft the stuff of the gods! When my nocker is in his Grump years I want some band of Wilders and childlings to come up his house at the end of their epic quest. I want to be something worth questing for not some glorified errandboy! I want my Squire to prove he is worthy of House Dougal by forging hisown blade.. or failing and being outcast an trying to find his place in the world. I want to forge a ring that can only be forged under the solstice Moon while all around me my Oathcircle defends me from those who would not see it done! I see no reason the forging fo the ring should &quot;just happen&quot; any more than a troll should &quot;just cleave an enemy in two&quot; because hey combat is boring right?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T01:38:03-07:00","id":970568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=970506#post970506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No. I'm saying No crafting system spits in the face of the Kith's concept. Each and every issue you have with a Crafting system could be applied to any other system. &amp;quot;We went of a quest and the nocker failed to smith our sword what bullshit&amp;quot; is no different than &amp;quot;We went on a quest and the Sluagh failed to sneak up on a dragon and we lost&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;We challenged the evil Duke.. and he beat us with swords what bullshit&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> You think Crafting was the place for munchkining not.. COMBAT in D&amp;D? <br /> <br /> <br /> A system is only as boring as you make it. You say its dramatic to go in a quest. I say the drama is in the forge. To do the impossible by the skin of your teeth to become a person who can craft the stuff of the gods! When my nocker is in his Grump years I want some band of Wilders and childlings to come up his house at the end of their epic quest. I want to be something worth questing for not some glorified errandboy! I want my Squire to prove he is worthy of House Dougal by forging hisown blade.. or failing and being outcast an trying to find his place in the world. I want to forge a ring that can only be forged under the solstice Moon while all around me my Oathcircle defends me from those who would not see it done! I see no reason the forging fo the ring should &amp;quot;just happen&amp;quot; any more than a troll should &amp;quot;just cleave an enemy in two&amp;quot; because hey combat is boring right?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it's a matter of balance. It's not always suitable to stage an epic quest every time a character wants to forge a new chimerical sword. In those instances, use the mechanics. But where the crafting of the sword itself tells an interesting story, then turn it into a quest and roleplay it.<br /> <br /> Remember that one of the key things to know as a Storyteller is when to call for a roll or not. If the characters have completed that quest magnificently, it'd be a shame to say they fail because of a bad roll. If the quest was roleplayed well I won't call for a roll at all.<br /> <br /> But there's such a thing as downtime. Sometimes you don't have time for roleplaying how everyone accounts for every item in their possession. So just make some rolls, spend some XP and add a brief description to your blue book or character sheet. Then it's done.<br /> <br /> Take, as an example, the hunting rules of VTM. If a vampire seduces a human in a club and drinks their blood, you don't need to make a hunting roll as well. But when you need to handwave the process, the hunting roll is a good way to do so fairly.<br /> <br /> The other thing to consider is balance. I.e., is it fair if the only rules in the book are for combat? Most Storyteller Dramatic Systems chapters relate to combat, car chases and cinematic explosions. It's a legacy from wargames, but it suggests an emphasis on combat to some players. In recent years OPP (like the rest of the RPG industry) has come to recognise this imbalance and has worked to better balance those systems. <br /> <br /> Not every player is equally good at roleplaying social encounters, for example. In a way, forcing people to roleplay social interaction, or giving such rules short thrift, disadvantages some types of player and discourages some character builds. So those players might want a system for settling social combat. Likewise, forging treasures. Not every player will be expert at handling that as a roleplaying thing. Nor should they need to.<br /> <br /> Besides, all these subsystems will always be options. They're there if you need them and you're encouraged to use them only when appropriate. It's better to have them just in case. You're not forced to use them, but they might come in useful to someone. As Lian pointed out, people don't always want to (or can) create systems on the fly for every eventuality. Better that the rulebook give you a helping hand--after all, that's why we're paying for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T08:35:05-07:00","id":970716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=970568#post970568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say it's a matter of balance. It's not always suitable to stage an epic quest every time a character wants to forge a new chimerical sword. In those instances, use the mechanics. But where the crafting of the sword itself tells an interesting story, then turn it into a quest and roleplay it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am denying the idea that the quest has to be the &quot;Dramatic&quot; part and the Crafting is just an after thought. You can easily focus on the drama of the craft itself, ESPECIALLY when its litterally the stuff of dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T00:10:55-07:00","id":971192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=970716#post970716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am denying the idea that the quest has to be the &amp;quot;Dramatic&amp;quot; part and the Crafting is just an after thought. You can easily focus on the drama of the craft itself, ESPECIALLY when its litterally the stuff of dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Although, it wouldn't be my idea of fun. 'You hammer. Then hammer for a bit longer. Then a bit more. Turn the heat up. Hammer again...' Etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T01:11:59-07:00","id":971198,"title":"","content":"Well, it's a good thing practically every writer, poet, and filmmaker disagrees about how epically dramatic crafting is, in and of itself. The two best known examples of crafting in &quot;modern&quot; film are the swords from the start of Conan ('80s) and Kill Bill. The former is done under the credits as a montage lasting less than 3 minutes, and the former is handled like this: &quot;It will take me a month to make the sword.&quot; Fade to black. Big titles: One Month Later. Also the Conan remake, which handled it in under a minute. Yeah, that's some epicly epicness that needs pages and charts. <br /> <br /> I get that it's your favorite thing and all, but that's word count that should go towards things that more people actually need and more people would actually use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T02:53:38-07:00","id":971226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=971198#post971198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's a good thing practically every writer, poet, and filmmaker disagrees about how epically dramatic crafting is, in and of itself. The two best known examples of crafting in &amp;quot;modern&amp;quot; film are the swords from the start of Conan ('80s) and Kill Bill. The former is done under the credits as a montage lasting less than 3 minutes, and the former is handled like this: &amp;quot;It will take me a month to make the sword.&amp;quot; Fade to black. Big titles: One Month Later. Also the Conan remake, which handled it in under a minute. Yeah, that's some epicly epicness that needs pages and charts. <br /> <br /> I get that it's your favorite thing and all, but that's word count that should go towards things that more people actually need and more people would actually use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it could be fun for someone, I guess, which is why I think both options are valid. But the tables and charts mean you *don't* have to spend loads of narrative time on it. So I'm with you that crafting doesn't need loads of time, but still for the crafting subsystems. In another game, I'd agree that they're extraneous. But there's a whole kith around crafting and Treasures are invaluable in making up for naff Arts. So having a decent system to account for what nockers actually do means you don't have to turn the crafting process into a story of its own. Roll a few dice and it's done, and still dramatically interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:26:30-07:00","id":971384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=971198#post971198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's a good thing practically every writer, poet, and filmmaker disagrees about how epically dramatic crafting is, in and of itself. The two best known examples of crafting in &quot;modern&quot; film are the swords from the start of Conan ('80s) and Kill Bill. The former is done under the credits as a montage lasting less than 3 minutes, and the former is handled like this: &quot;It will take me a month to make the sword.&quot; Fade to black. Big titles: One Month Later. Also the Conan remake, which handled it in under a minute. Yeah, that's some epicly epicness that needs pages and charts.<br /> <br /> I get that it's your favorite thing and all, but that's word count that should go towards things that more people actually need and more people would actually use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Star trek Episode where they need to Fix or Build something, most Notably Star Trek 2, which comes down to whether Spock can make the right Crafting Roll before he dies. Every Episode of Macguyver. Iron Man, Iron Man 3. Captain America.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand we have pages and pages of charts for something that is the most banal thing out there. Combat. Have you seen CWOD combat? Its not This <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lC6dgtBU6Gs\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lC6dgtBU6Gs</a> its &quot;I go first, you die&quot; No wit. No words. No banter. It agressively promotes ambushes,overwhelming force and extra Actions. HOW BORING! So I assume you want them to completely rework all the rules for that right? Adding Stunts, changing mechanics, a complete and utter overhaul of the system from the ground up to make combat dramatic. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:37:46-07:00","id":971392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=971384#post971384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I assume you want them to completely rework all the rules for that right? Adding Stunts, changing mechanics, a complete and utter overhaul of the system from the ground up to make combat dramatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a tangent, but... I would <i>love</i> to see combat become something less cumbersome mechanically and be more cinematic, but still be over the top and dramatic.<br /> <br /> My big hope for 5th edition WoD is that the core system gets back to its roots rejecting complicated, cumbersome systems and becomes more light weight and narrative based.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:43:14-07:00","id":971396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=971392#post971392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a tangent, but... I would <i>love</i> to see combat become something less cumbersome mechanically and be more cinematic, but still be over the top and dramatic.<br /> <br /> My big hope for 5th edition WoD is that the core system gets back to its roots rejecting complicated, cumbersome systems and becomes more light weight and narrative based.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's an issue. Should Combat be &quot;Gritty&quot; or &quot;Cinematic&quot; for vampire it feels like surprise Murder should be the way to do it. Changeling I feel like most of their fights should be like something out of movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:36:16-07:00","id":971464,"title":"","content":"I think there's space for both. Requiem does gritty pretty well. Masquerade is my go to for cinematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:48:51-07:00","id":971468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=971464#post971464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's space for both. Requiem does gritty pretty well. Masquerade is my go to for cinematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Masquerade isn't even close to my go to for cinematic. Its much closer to an elaborate murder system outside wiffing. The general weakness of defense promotes alpha strikes which.. while &quot;Realistic&quot; isn't particularly cinematic.<br /> <br /> Even older larp which moved the balance the other way just lead to &quot;Silver bullet&quot; combat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T13:00:01-07:00","id":971480,"title":"","content":"I should note, when I run classic World of Darkness, the rules are much more of a suggestion than something I follow. I pretty much always ignore the complicated fiddly bits and subsystems. A roll or two with whatever attribute and ability combination seems appropriate at the time is usually all I ever need. A couple of my players were pretty amazed at how many rules actually exist when I ran the C20 play test sessions since I made a point to run those by the book.<br /> <br /> I have a much harder time doing that with Chronicles of Darkness and tend to run it pretty much rules as written. I have no idea why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T13:18:58-07:00","id":971488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=971480#post971480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should note, when I run classic World of Darkness, the rules are much more of a suggestion than something I follow. I pretty much always ignore the complicated fiddly bits and subsystems. A roll or two with whatever attribute and ability combination seems appropriate at the time is usually all I ever need. A couple of my players were pretty amazed at how many rules actually exist when I ran the C20 play test sessions since I made a point to run those by the book.<br /> <br /> I have a much harder time doing that with Chronicles of Darkness and tend to run it pretty much rules as written. I have no idea why.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe if I started tossign around banality/glamour for action. It might change things up for changelings... like giving someone banality automatically for pullign the invisible sniper.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T16:00:05-07:00","id":971556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=971392#post971392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a tangent, but... I would <i>love</i> to see combat become something less cumbersome mechanically and be more cinematic, but still be over the top and dramatic.<br /> <br /> My big hope for 5th edition WoD is that the core system gets back to its roots rejecting complicated, cumbersome systems and becomes more light weight and narrative based.</div> </div> </div> </div>If only. Hell, I'm hoping they do a 4th/5th edition of all the lines. Clearly there's still demand for the oWoD. If nothing else the V4/5 basics could be ported to C20. I would also love to see some non-house system books for the lines. Like a Fate, Savage Worlds, and Apocalypse Engine book released for the oWoD lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T23:17:27-07:00","id":972363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=971556#post971556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If only. Hell, I'm hoping they do a 4th/5th edition of all the lines. Clearly there's still demand for the oWoD. If nothing else the V4/5 basics could be ported to C20. I would also love to see some non-house system books for the lines. Like a Fate, Savage Worlds, and Apocalypse Engine book released for the oWoD lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because my roleplaying experience starts and ends with oWoD (with a bit of Unknown Armies, Fading Suns and Over the Edge), I recently tried to broaden my horizons with the D&amp;D Starter Kit and Shadowrun Beginner's Box. I thought, 'These should be easy enough to start a one-shot with this weekend...' Then I started reading the rules!<br /> <br /> D&amp;D can't even use one type of dice and Shadowrun combat involves so many details! D&amp;D, especially, felt like a wargame with all of its rules for movement; and Shadowrun just overcomplicates combat to the point it kills the fun (ahem). Instead, I rediscovered the elegant glamour of the CTD Quickstart and thought, 'Now that's a good system for beginners!'<br /> <br /> Suffice it to say, I'm gonna hack both games to bits before I start either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 09-19-2016, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T09:29:34-07:00","id":972573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=972363#post972363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because my roleplaying experience starts and ends with oWoD (with a bit of Unknown Armies, Fading Suns and Over the Edge), I recently tried to broaden my horizons with the D&amp;D Starter Kit and Shadowrun Beginner's Box. I thought, 'These should be easy enough to start a one-shot with this weekend...' Then I started reading the rules!</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. You went straight for two rules medium - rules heavy games and were hoping for a quick one shot over the weekend. That sucks. Check out Fate Accelerated, the whole thing is something like 50 pages long and freely available online (legally). There's also Simple World, a 10-page generic version of the Apocalypse Engine. Hell, there's also Risus, a 6-page game that can do just about anything, though it's generally used for comedy games. Cthulhu Dark is a 4-page game that does Lovecraftian horror quite well. World of Dungeons is a 3-page Apocalypse Engine hack for playing D&amp;D-like fantasy. Or Lasers &amp; Feelings, a 1-page game that is meant for Star Trek, but can really do anything by finding to two opposing modes of action and renaming the stats, such as Go Quiet &amp; Go Loud for Shadowrun, or Mortal &amp; Fae for Changeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> D&amp;D can't even use one type of dice and Shadowrun combat involves so many details! D&amp;D, especially, felt like a wargame with all of its rules for movement; and Shadowrun just overcomplicates combat to the point it kills the fun (ahem). Instead, I rediscovered the elegant glamour of the CTD Quickstart and thought, 'Now that's a good system for beginners!'<br /> <br /> Suffice it to say, I'm gonna hack both games to bits before I start either. </div> </div> </div>Just because the system is small and focused, don't assume it's only for beginners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T01:24:22-07:00","id":972993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=972573#post972573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. You went straight for two rules medium - rules heavy games and were hoping for a quick one shot over the weekend. That sucks. Check out Fate Accelerated, the whole thing is something like 50 pages long and freely available online (legally). There's also Simple World, a 10-page generic version of the Apocalypse Engine. Hell, there's also Risus, a 6-page game that can do just about anything, though it's generally used for comedy games. Cthulhu Dark is a 4-page game that does Lovecraftian horror quite well. World of Dungeons is a 3-page Apocalypse Engine hack for playing D&amp;D-like fantasy. Or Lasers &amp; Feelings, a 1-page game that is meant for Star Trek, but can really do anything by finding to two opposing modes of action and renaming the stats, such as Go Quiet &amp; Go Loud for Shadowrun, or Mortal &amp; Fae for Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>The boxes are labelled 'Starter Kit' and 'Beginner's Box'. They're ostensibly for newbies, or else they're marketing themselves badly. The boxes say there's everything included to start playing quickly, but the rules just don't allow for that. Shadowrun wasn't too bad, but combat looks bogged down in lots of math. D&amp;D probably should have just thrown out all the microdetails for the Starter Kit and saved them for the core books.<br /> <br /> For Shadowrun, I'll probably use their own traits but Storyteller mechanics (combat especially). For D&amp;D I have seen some hacks online that look simple enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because the system is small and focused, don't assume it's only for beginners. </div> </div> </div>Of course it isn't, but it's very well suited to beginners. I could show that to my non-RPGer friends (who are familiar with board games but can't figure out what an RPG actually is), and they'd get the rules straight away. The setting I'd just show them through play.<br /> <br /> You have four Traits, Basic and Advanced Arts, and a few pools of points. Combat is super-quick, there's no rolling for initiative, weapon damage is so easy it's ridiculous, and the result is a surprisingly robust set of rules with a tiny learning curve.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we're kinda getting off-topic, but I was trying to say that the elegance of the Storyteller system is easy to overlook until you consider the complexity of some of the others. I like having optional rules every now and again for dramatic, game-like tension, but mostly I just need something simple that doesn't get in the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:53:04-07:00","id":973492,"title":"","content":"There are only two things that I expect to be completely overhauled in C20: the Cantrip System and the &quot;How to Get Glamour System&quot;.<br /> I hope they improve and develop the rest, but more like polishing what we've already had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:34:52-07:00","id":973871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=973492#post973492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are only two things that I expect to be completely overhauled in C20: the Cantrip System and the &amp;quot;How to Get Glamour System&amp;quot;.<br /> I hope they improve and develop the rest, but more like polishing what we've already had.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you'll mostly get what you want. Have you seen the excerpt from the cantrips system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:38:47-07:00","id":973976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=972363#post972363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> D&amp;D can't even use one type of dice and Shadowrun combat involves so many details! D&amp;D, especially, felt like a wargame with all of its rules for movement; and Shadowrun just overcomplicates combat to the point it kills the fun (ahem). Instead, I rediscovered the elegant glamour of the CTD Quickstart and thought, 'Now that's a good system for beginners!'<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, I always thought it funny the DnD crowd preaches 5e for being rules light and story focused for some ideas WoD did decades ago. Meanwhile a lot of people here and rpg.net curses WoD for being clunky and complicated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well, perspectives, as always. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: and we didn't go into Pathfinder-land... (which i also like for its own merits).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The boxes are labelled 'Starter Kit' and 'Beginner's Box'. They're ostensibly for newbies, or else they're marketing themselves badly. The boxes say there's everything included to start playing quickly, but the rules just don't allow for that. Shadowrun wasn't too bad, but combat looks bogged down in lots of math. D&amp;D probably should have just thrown out all the microdetails for the Starter Kit and saved them for the core books. </div> </div> </div>What do you consider &quot;quickly&quot;? I'm not meaning it in a sarcastic way, just genuinely wondering about how different people see these things, since I never considered a few hours-couple of days digesting the rules prior to gaming as a really significant investment. Admittedly I'm not really into extremely rules-light systems, I think at that point we could just do freeform, or party games. As a matter of fact, I somewhat consider those as the party games of rpg, which is good it has it's own niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 09-21-2016, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:04:28-07:00","id":973989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=973976#post973976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh, I always thought it funny the DnD crowd preaches 5e for being rules light and story focused for some ideas WoD did decades ago. Meanwhile a lot of people here and rpg.net curses WoD for being clunky and complicated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well, perspectives, as always. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: and we didn't go into Pathfinder-land... (which i also like for its own merits).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What do you consider &amp;quot;quickly&amp;quot;? I'm not meaning it in a sarcastic way, just genuinely wondering about how different people see these things, since I never considered a few hours-couple of days digesting the rules prior to gaming as a really significant investment. Admittedly I'm not really into extremely rules-light systems, I think at that point we could just do freeform, or party games. As a matter of fact, I somewhat consider those as the party games of rpg, which is good it has it's own niche.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expected a couple of hours, tops, but I was planning on running it the next morning with complete newbies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:19:16-07:00","id":973998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/968289-c20-minor-tweaks-to-a-nostalgia-product-vs-a-more-drastic-overhaul?p=973989#post973989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I expected a couple of hours, tops, but I was planning on running it the next morning with complete newbies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay, then I could relate with the disappointment! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I didn't read the starter box rules, but I thought the PHB is doable as a fairly fast and light thing without the elaborated combat rules in the DMG and without feats/multiclassing and taking the simpler class archetypes. Even grid isn't as &quot;necessary&quot; as in former editions. I thought the starter set took that way to keep it to the minimum. I'd give it a couple of days to digest it although, before DMing it.<br /> <br /> The again, my reference point is DnD 3e, so 5e seemed fairly simple, even with all the bells and whistles (and as such, DnD isn't a whole new system for me) and WoD laughably so (except Mage, but it's somewhat the point, IMO).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 09-21-2016, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}